.TH SDL_CreateSoftwareRenderer 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateSoftwareRenderer \- Create a 2D software rendering context for a surface.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Renderer * SDL_CreateSoftwareRenderer(SDL_Surface *surface);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Two other APIs which can be used to create
.BR SDL_Renderer :
.BR SDL_CreateRenderer ()
and
.BR SDL_CreateWindowAndRenderer ()\[char46]
These can _also_ create a software renderer, but they are intended to be used with an
.BR SDL_Window
as the final destination and not an
.BR SDL_Surface \[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I surface
the surface where rendering is done, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid rendering context or NULL if there was an error; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_DestroyRenderer (3),
.BR SDL_SetSoftwareRendererSurface (3),
.BR SDL_SetSoftwareRendererWindow (3)
